# Slice 282 probe: a typed path through a rebound callable reads the field of the callable that stands there, by its name, not by the position in the callable the path was typed by.  Entry 7.
Callables:
    fn: f () int
        int: x 3
        return: x
    end: f
end: Callables
fn: replaced () int
    int: y 9
    int: x 7
    return: x
end: replaced
int: code 7
if: Callables\f() != 3
    code: 11
---
if: code = 7 && Callables\f\x != 3
    code: 12
---
@: Callables\f replaced
if: code = 7 && Callables\f() != 7
    code: 13
---
if: code = 7 && Callables\f\x != 7
    code: 14
---
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: code; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
